= Open access — Simple =

Open access is an access and reuse model for scholarly outputs that makes them available online without price barriers and, under stronger definitions, with broad permissions for lawful reuse.

Open-access routes can include publication by an open-access venue or deposit in a repository. Access conditions and reuse rights depend on licenses, publisher policies, repository terms, and the specific open-access model.

'''Important boundaries:'''
* open access ≠ open science
* free-to-read ≠ unrestricted reuse necessarily

